{"availability":"available","full":"alexk111/One-Time-Address","name":"One-Time-Address","description":"🏷 A better way to share your Bitcoin address.","category":"Other","language":"Handlebars","stars":82,"forks":7,"created":"2019-08-25T12:01:03Z","updated":"2022-12-11T04:04:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["bitcoin","bitcoin-address","bitcoin-payment","payments"],"demo":"https://donate.alexkaul.com/one-time-address","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:22.590Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:22.590Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:22.590Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:22.590Z","stars":82,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["One-Time Address is a self-hosted, open-source service which turns your Bitcoin wallets into webpages and embeddable widgets that instantly provide an address with a QR code whenever someone wants to send you Bitcoin.","One-Time Address never shows the same address twice and thus helps to prevent address reuse. You should not reuse addresses because it abuses the privacy and security of the participants of the transactions as well as future holders of their value.","Note #1: If the same visitor requests an address multiple times within a short period, he might see an address generated for him last time instead of a new one. This prevents wallets from bloating with repetitive requests."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alexk111/One-Time-Address/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"0107235de30c0d0e69969e8dd8f19f97b69795c165d85635a0b0f17096758884","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:22.695Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:22.695Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"One-Time Address is a self-hosted, open-source service which turns your Bitcoin wallets into webpages and embeddable widgets that instantly provide an address with a QR code whenever someone wants to send you Bitcoin.","sourceUrl"